From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:56:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build the riscv64-to-x86_64 intrinsics generator as a stub on
 arm64 hosts

gen_riscv64_to_x86_64_intrinsics runs on the build host, and its genrule
exists on every build, but berberis disables arm64, so an arm64 host
stopped at analysis with a dependency on a disabled module. Give arm64
Linux hosts the dummy generator that darwin already uses, and keep the
real one on x86_64. Its header only feeds the x86_64 translator.

Change-Id: I0dcc5f178b0b5ee520e8d052a686215cc8eabe05
---
 intrinsics/Android.bp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/intrinsics/Android.bp b/intrinsics/Android.bp
index 2b1f4df..e1f78b8 100644
--- a/intrinsics/Android.bp
+++ b/intrinsics/Android.bp
@@ -248,7 +248,7 @@ cc_binary_host {
     defaults: ["gen_text_asm_intrinsics_defaults"],
     local_include_dirs: ["riscv64_to_x86_64"],
     target: {
-        linux: {
+        linux_x86_64: {
             generated_headers: [
                 "libberberis_intrinsics_gen_public_headers_riscv64_to_x86_64",
                 "libberberis_macro_assembler_gen_intrinsics_headers_riscv64_to_x86_64",
@@ -285,7 +285,13 @@ cc_defaults {
             enabled: true,
             srcs: [":dummy_gen_text_asm_intrinsics_srcs"],
         },
-        linux: {
+        // An arm64 build host never builds the x86_64 translator these
+        // headers are for.
+        linux_arm64: {
+            enabled: true,
+            srcs: [":dummy_gen_text_asm_intrinsics_srcs"],
+        },
+        linux_x86_64: {
             // We are only ever executing that binary once, it's faster to build it without
             // optimizations and spend half-second more running it, than spend tens of seconds
             // optimizing the code to save that half-second.
